# LeetCode 167. Two Sum II - Input Array Is Sorted
# https://leetcode.com/problems/two-sum-ii-input-array-is-sorted/
#
# Approach: Two-pointer technique. Since the array is sorted, start pointers
# at both ends. If the sum is too small, move left pointer right to increase
# the sum. If too big, move right pointer left to decrease it.

Here was my initial solution
def twoSum(self, numbers, target):
        left, right = 0, len(numbers) - 1


        while left < right:
            if numbers[left] + numbers[right] == target:
                return [left + 1, right + 1]
            elif numbers[left] + numbers[right] > target:
                right -= 1
            else:
                left += 1
A bug I ran into was i was incrementing and decrementing the values of the array and not the pointer index itself
